1. lyk-steno-theory (derived code)
----------------------------------

Upstream:  lyk-steno-theory, https://github.com/noahlyk/lyk-steno-theory
Copyright: noahlyk (the author of both projects)
License:   GNU GPL version 3 or later

The adaptive test (the word feed, the vocabulary and its rules, the typing engine and the
results screen: `src/practice/`, `src/vocab.rs`) was extracted from lyk-steno-theory's
`lyk practice` and `lyk vocab` and made engine-agnostic. The format of `vocab.json` is the same,
so a lyk vocabulary loads unchanged.

2. Monkeytype word lists (downloaded, and the 200-word list built in)
---------------------------------------------------------------------

Upstream:  Monkeytype, https://github.com/monkeytypegame/monkeytype
           (frontend/static/languages/english*.json)
License:   GNU GPL version 3

`typeladder fetch` (and the first run) downloads the lists `english`, `english_1k`,
`english_5k`, `english_10k`, `english_25k` and `english_450k` into the data folder.
`assets/monkeytype-english.json` is a copy of the 200-word `english` list, built into the
program so the first run works offline.

3. Monkeytype's results screen (a design reference only)
--------------------------------------------------------

The results screen imitates the layout of Monkeytype's (big wpm and accuracy, a chart, character
counts); no Monkeytype code is used for it.
